# .cursorrules — Velora

## Read first
docs/ARCHITECTURE.md · docs/DESIGN-SPEC.md · docs/PHASES.md · prompts/00-KICKSTART.md
design/*.dc.html are design REFERENCES in HTML. Never copy their markup into the app.

## Stack (fixed)
Next.js 15 App Router · TypeScript strict · Tailwind v4 · Framer Motion + GSAP ScrollTrigger + Lenis ·
Firebase Firestore (+ Auth for admin only) · ImageKit · Server Actions / Route Handlers (no Cloud Functions) ·
Razorpay · Shiprocket · Resend · Cloudflare Pages/Workers.
Do not add a dependency without stating why in one line.

## Layering (MVVM) — enforced
view -> viewmodel -> model. One direction only.
- model/**: domain entities, Zod schemas, repository INTERFACES, domain services. No react, no next/*, no firebase.
- infrastructure/**: implements repository interfaces. The only place SDKs appear.
- viewmodel/**: server view models (async, called by page.tsx), client hooks, Server Actions.
- view/**: presentation only. Props in, JSX out. No fetching, no business rules, no SDK imports.
Violations that are bugs: a component importing firebase/*; a repository returning a DocumentSnapshot;
UI copy hardcoded in JSX; money as a float; business rules inside view/.

## Money
Integer paise only, `Paise` branded type. Format in a `Price` primitive. Recompute amounts server-side; never
trust a client-sent total.

## Design rules
Palette: cream #FDF4E4 · saffron #E8621B · marigold #F5A623 · turmeric #F8CE5A · pressed #B4470F ·
ink #241F1C · sand #F6EAD6 · peacock #12514E (WhatsApp only).
No wine, no crimson, no brown fields, no logo gradients, no shadows, no border-radius except circles.
Deep saree hues (maroon/peacock/indigo/leaf/plum/kora) are product data only, never chrome.
Type: Bodoni Moda display + wordmark (.28em, compensate margin-right:-.28em), Archivo body/UI,
Anek Tamil for Tamil. Endorsement "by Bharani Pattu" under the wordmark in header and footer, always.
Tokens come from globals.css; never hardcode a hex in a component.

## Motion
Easing cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); durations 600–900ms; values only from lib/motion.ts.
Nothing bounces or springs. Every moment has a prefers-reduced-motion branch.
No animation may delay the first product image.

## Mobile first
390 is the primary design; 1440 is the widened version. 44px minimum touch targets, 48/56px buttons.
Sticky bottom bar screens reserve ~96px bottom padding on the scrolling column; any block under the
WhatsApp FAB reserves a ~60px right gutter. Verify at 390x844 explicitly.

## Performance budget (a hard constraint)
LCP < 2.5s on 4G, CLS < 0.05. Hero poster is a real <img fetchpriority="high">; video attaches after LCP.
Drape loops 3s, <=400 KB, muted playsinline preload="none", mounted within one viewport.
GSAP + pallu scroll are desktop-only and dynamically imported. If a moment costs 300ms of LCP, cut it and say so.

## Data + safety
Every saree is one physical unit; reservations use a Firestore transaction with a 15-minute lock.
`timeline` is append-only and is the only source for tracking UI.
Order state changes go through model/service/orderStateMachine.ts — invalid transitions throw.
Payments: verify signatures server-side with timingSafeEqual on the raw body; webhooks idempotent by event id;
one `settlePayment()` is the only place an order becomes paid.
No secrets in the client bundle. No PII in logs. Structured logs only: { event, orderId?, sareeId?, ms }.

## AI-readiness
Entities expose toEmbeddingText(). sarees/{id}/ai reserved, unwritten. Merchandising copy in Firestore.
All writes via Server Actions with Zod schemas in model/schema (these double as future agent tools).
Bilingual fields paired (titleEn/titleTa).

## Process
Phases in order: UI -> backend -> integration -> payments -> tracking. Do not scaffold a later phase early.
Before each phase, restate the plan as a file checklist and wait for approval.
TypeScript strict, no `any`, no non-null `!` outside tests. Small conventional commits, one concern each.
When the design is ambiguous, ask — do not invent a new visual pattern.
